.claude/
backups/

# real annual roster corrections stay on the machine, never in public Git
scripts/roster-*.local.json

# patches are transport, not source
*.patch
# old build zips - they contain real student names
*.zip

# rendered by test/progress-report.browser.mjs, regenerated on every run
server/progress-report.png
server/progress-report.sample.html

server/nastava-page.png

# Generated architecture maps in root must not be scanned as app
/mtb-seams.html

# files Claude delivers into the chat land here on this machine; they are
# evidence for a conversation, not source, and one of them is a PNG the name
# guard then has to open on every commit
Claude outputs/

# agent tooling installed per machine, not part of the apps. `.agents/skills/`
# holds third-party skill packs (HyperFrames et al.) and `skills-lock.json`
# is their manifest; both arrive by installer, differ between HOME and WORK,
# and a single `git add -A` would put dozens of vendor directories into a
# public repository that serves GitHub Pages.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
